            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "[Only local file system](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/ccfc6300a5c17387f2899f979ecc04f942bee2a0/doc/mini-files.txt#L30) is planned to be supported. I am not *actually* opposed to to having 'mini.files' work over SSH, but only if the cost is relatively low (in terms of code complexity and size). For example, if there will be such functions in Neovim core (maybe support through `vim.fs`), I'd adapt 'mini.files' accordingly.",
